Others: Mona Singh, SBC Specialist, Bihar 
Nishant Shukla, Ministry of Health and Family Welfare Jaishri Jethwaney, Senior Advisor – Communications (ITSU), MOHFW. 8. Policy implications and recommendations

The objective of this evaluation exercise was to understand the SBCC Cells’ performance towards maximizing utilization of allocated resources and augmenting the results of the health systems strengthening initiatives and other cross sectoral themes of social and health determinants at the state and district level. A qualitative research design was adopted for the same. Findings from this study have provided insights into the status of the existing SBCC cells and identified certain areas for improvement in its functioning. The suggestive recommendations for strengthening the functioning of SBCC cells are based on the findings from study, field observations, consultations with stakeholders. Confidence in the generalizability of the findings and recommendations is enhanced by the comprehensive strategy and design used for the selection of the states and arena of stakeholders interviewed as a part of this evaluation . Recommendation 1:

